WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- So, are you amazed
with how much, I mean,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.230
people still love "The
Notebook", they still talk.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.060
It's just one of the most
gigantic love stories.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.950
Did you know, did you have an inkling that

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.100
this is gonna connect
when you were writing it?

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.470
It's hard to say, I guess, now.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.640
- You know, when I was writing it,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.080
I thought it had a chance.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:16.980
It was funny, you know.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.610
It was a story originally inspired

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.800
by my wife at the time,
Kathy, her grandparents.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.010
And I remember seeing how
much they cared for each other

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.060
toward the end of their life,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.100
and it was a story that moved me.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.813
And as I'm there typing,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.240
I hoped people would get
it, but one never knows.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.073
- You don't, yeah.

00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:37.980
- I had no agent.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:38.940
I knew nothing about

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.686
publishing at the time.
- Wow, geez.

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:41.519
- I was working.
- What?

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:42.352
I didn't know that.
- Yeah, I was working

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.185
full time.

00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:45.750
And then we had a young baby at the time

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:46.800
who didn't sleep well,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.510
so I had time in the evening to write

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.370
since Kathy would go to sleep.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.970
And, so I wrote "The
Notebook" in my spare time.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.740
- In your spare time.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.873
Just wrote "The Notebook", it's fine.

